'''Pinky''' is one of the two major protagonists in [[Pinky and the Brain (segment)|the ''Pinky and the Brain'' segments]] seen in both [[Animaniacs]] [[Animaniacs (2020 TV series)|shows]], as well as its [[Pinky and the Brain|spinoff]] [[Pinky, Elmyra and the Brain|shows]]. Pinky is an open-minded, often nonsensical lab mouse and the assistant and roommate of [[The Brain]], who often blames Pinky for the failure of his [[Brain's Plans|plans]].

He is voiced by [[Rob Paulsen]].

==Appearance==

Pinky is a tall, anthropomorphic white-furred mouse; in the ''Animaniacs'' reboot, his fur is more off-white. He has large ears, a red nose, and pink skin on his paws and straight tail. He has two protruding front teeth, and blue eyes. He also has three tufts of fur atop his head as a distinguishing feature.

In the original ''Animaniacs'' and ''Pinky and the Brain'' spin-off, Pinky is two years old.<ref name="patb christmas">[[Episode 8 (PATB): A Pinky and the Brain Christmas]]</ref> By the 2020 ''Animaniacs'' reboot, he is three.<ref name="mouse congeniality">[[Episode 19 (Reboot): Yakko's Big Idea/Mouse Congeniality/Rejected Animaniacs Characters|Episode 19B (Reboot)]]: "[[Mouse Congeniality]]"</ref> This is most likely in Rodent Years. His name comes from the term for a baby or young mouse.

==Personality==
Described in the intro as "insane," Pinky is both eagerly optimistic and entirely oblivious to most everything happening around him. He is often very unfocused, naive, and forgetful, as well as friendly, open-minded and loyal. He is almost always happy and hyperactive, and seems to live in his own little world inside his head. He has a huge but unconventional imagination, often leading those around him to not understand what he's talking about; his lack of focus also prevents him from realizing how many of the things he says and does would seem random.<ref name="pinky p.o.v.">[[Episode 58 (PATB): The Pinky P.O.V./The Really Great Dictator/Brain Food|Episode 58A (PATB)]]: "[[The Pinky P.O.V.]]"</ref> His scatter-brained personality often helps him stay optimistic in times of trouble, though it can also get him into worse situations– for instance, he often finds himself chewing electrical wires or unable to remember to breathe.

[[File:Pinky Acme Labs Report.jpg|thumb|250x250px|left|Lab report on Pinky|alt=]]Despite Brain's belief that Pinky is a complete idiot, Pinky does excel in his own unique forms of intelligence; he can name all the world's cheeses, including which country produces each type, and has a large knowledge of popular culture (being television in the original shows and internet sensations and webseries in the reboot). While his social skills are lacking, he often finds himself the more popular one of the duo, very quickly making friends or allies who are intrigued by his strange way of thinking. In "[[Episode 17 (PATB): The Pink Candidate|The Pink Candidate]]," he also showed himself to be a fair and honest leader, and "[[Episode 19 (PATB): Welcome to the Jungle|Welcome to the Jungle]]" showcased that Pinky is very quick to adapt and improvise in unusual circumstances. There have also been cases where Pinky has used his unique ideas to almost overtake the world faster than Brain, such as "[[Episode 31 (PATB): All You Need Is Narf/Pinky's Plan#Pinky's Plan|Pinky's Plan]]" and "[[Episode 54 (PATB): Pinky's Turn/Your Friend: Global Domination#Pinky's Turn|Pinky's Turn]]," only for Brain to accidentally ruin the attempt. 

Pinky enjoys sensations that others would find painful, such as when Brain bops him on the head, or running into glass,<ref name="snowball" /><ref name="brainwashed3" /> though he also has other, less dangerous repetitive movements he enjoys, such as bouncing, running on their hamster wheel, and dancing. Most notably, there are several "nonsense" words that he often repeats or throws into conversations; in "[[Episode 58 (PATB): The Pinky P.O.V./The Really Great Dictator/Brain Food#The Pinky P.O.V.|The Pinky P.O.V.]]", it is shown that he visualizes these words appearing in thin air as he speaks them. His most prominent word is "Narf," though he also often uses "Poit," "Zort," "Troz" ("Zort" spelled backwards) and "Fiddlely-posh," uses "Egad" as an exclamation, and will sometimes say "Zort" as a giveaway for when he is lying.<ref name="run pinky run">[[Episode 16 (Reboot): Rug of War/Run Pinky Run/The Hamburg Tickler|Episode 16B (Reboot)]]: "[[Run Pinky Run]]"</ref> He also has pica,<ref name="narf over troubled water" /> which means he often eats items generally considered inedible.

Pinky tends to fall in love easily, and usually with someone unexpected as regarded by society, such as [[Phar Fignewton]] (a horse, and his recurring girlfriend), a sea lion named Winnie, a pig named Penny, Brain's monster creation [[Drusilla]], an octopus, or a sock puppet. 

Quite often, he dresses and acts in a gender non-comforming way, often dressing in drag either for one of his and Brain's plans or simply because he wants to. He also enjoys playing with makeup and wearing fancy dresses. He shows no dislike for being referred to by "she/her" pronouns and in fact at one point says he has dreamed of being "the most beautiful human woman on the planet."<ref name="mouse congeniality" />

Pinky also may have some form of psychic powers; in the episode "[[Episode 11 (PATB): Fly|Fly]]," a distracted Pinky makes several pieces of fruit float with his mind. When asked how he does this, Pinky simply responds that it "comes and goes." He may also have regenerative abilities, as in another episode he suggests that he grew his leg back. 

His established character has changed a few times; in [[Episode 3 (PATB): Tokyo Grows/That Smarts/Brainstem#That Smarts|"That Smarts]]," Pinky temporarily became a genius like Brain, only for Pinky's new intelligence to cause a strain on their friendship after Pinky began pointing out all of the problems in his roommate's plans. He is also noted to be considerably ruder in ''[[Pinky, Elmyra and the Brain]]'', with Brain referring to him as a "hindrance with an attitude."<ref name="my fair brainy">[[Episode 3 (Elmyra): My Fair Brainy!/The Cat Who Cried Woof!|Episode 3A (Elmyra)]]: "[[My Fair Brainy!]]"</ref>

===Relationship with Brain===
[[File:Pinky-and-the-brain-rare-promo-art.jpeg|thumb|Brain and the Pinky]]
Pinky has a strong bond with his cagemate Brain, and thinks of him as his best friend. He is often very excited to help Brain with his ideas, even though he doesn't have an emotional stake in the idea of world domination, and does his best to help. Series creator [[Tom Ruegger]] has said, "Pinky's plans are really to hang out with Brain, have some fun, do something silly tonight about taking over the world and then get another food pellet."<ref name="realgenius">[https://melmagazine.com/en-us/story/pinky-and-the-brain-is-pinky-the-genius Mel - Is Pinky the Real Genius of 'Pinky and the Brain'? Their Creator Weighs In]</ref> Though his assistance often causes disaster, in other times he notices a plan's problem before Brain does, only to not be listened to. Pinky's excessive joy and distracted consciousness often annoy Brain, who constantly berates him or uses him for slapstick gags; while Pinky admits he's bothered by the insults, he actually enjoys the physical pain,<ref name="snowball">[[Episode 9 (PATB): Snowball]]</ref> which is shown to be true as he seems impervious to any kind of torture<ref name="patb halloween">[[Episode 42 (PATB): A Pinky and the Brain Halloween]]</ref> and sometimes actively seeks out activities that could prove harmful to others.<ref name="brainwashed3">[[Episode 61 (PATB): Brainwashed Part 3 - Wash Harder]]</ref> For his part, Brain is also very attached to Pinky, though his dislike of showing emotions prevents this side of him from being seen often. He has, however, been in great distress when Pinky is in danger,<ref name="welcome to the jungle">[[Episode 19 (PATB): Welcome to the Jungle]]</ref><ref name="future brain">[[Episode 9 (Reboot): Here Comes Treble/That's Not the Issue/Future Brain/The Incredible Gnome in People's Mouths|Episode 9C (Reboot)]]: "[[Future Brain]]"</ref> and literally went to [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hell hell] and back for him.<ref name="patb halloween" /> They are very loyal to each other despite their odd dynamic, and Pinky often functions as a moral compass for Brain, whether Brain likes it or not.

[[File:Thumbnailhulupatb52.png|thumb|left|250px|The awkward dinner date, from the episode "[[Brain's Night Off]]"]] 
While not directly stated in as many words, is also heavily implied that he harbors romantic feelings for Brain, as he often says vaguely flirtatious things towards his roommate, and several times has been portrayed as his spouse/partner during one of their plans<ref name="noah's lark">[[Episode 33: Cartoons in Wakko's Body/Noah's Lark/The Big Kiss/Hiccup|Episode 33B]]: "[[Noah's Lark]]"</ref> or, in some cases, a full sketch.<ref name="plight of hand">[[Episode 21 (Reboot): Wakkiver Twist Part One/Plight of Hand/Wakkiver Twist Part Two|Episode 21A and C (Reboot): "Wakkiver Twist"]]</ref><ref name="flawed couple">[[Episode 15 (Reboot): Please Submit/The Flawed Couple/Everyday Safety]]</ref> In "[[Episode 52 (PATB): Brain's Night Off/Beach Blanket Brain#Brain's Night Off|Brain's Night Off]]," the two of them go out to dinner on what seems to be a date, and Pinky has often fantasized about or paralleled acting as a housewife.<ref name="of mouse and man">[[Episode 2 (PATB): Of Mouse And Man]]</ref><ref name="pinky's dream house">[[Episode 6 (Elmyra): At the Hop!/Pinky's Dream House|Episode 6B (Elmyra)]]: "[[Pinky's Dream House]]"</ref><ref name="flawed couple" /> The pair have also stood in for love interests in multiple parodies, such as ''{{w|North by Northwest}},''<ref name="snowball" /> ''{{w|Run Lola Run}}''<ref name="run pinky run" />  and ''{{w|The Graduate}}.''<ref name="narf over troubled water" />

The two of them had a genetically-cloned child together, [[Romy]], and an episode entitled after their relationship name, "[[Episode 24 (PATB): Brinky|Brinky]]," in which Romy refers to him and Brain as his "two dads." In one of the ''Pinky and the Brain'' comics, Pinky became upset and jealous when Brain wouldn't let him play as Romy's mother.

